  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), る-ending.\n- Negative: {火照|ほて}らない\n- Polite: {火照|ほて}ります\n- Te-form: {火照|ほて}って\n- Past: {火照|ほて}った\n\nUSAGE:\nDescribes the sensation of warmth and redness in the skin. Common causes include embarrassment, alcohol, fever, bathing, and sun exposure. Often written in hiragana as ほてる.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {顔|かお}が{火照|ほて}る: face flushes\n- {体|からだ}が{火照|ほて}る: body feels hot\n- {火照|ほて}った{頬|ほお}: flushed cheeks\n\nHOMOPHONE NOTE:\nNot to be confused with ホテル (hotel), which is a loanword.",
